{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct divergence witness appeared: the two nodes hold different entries at the same index 8 s after healing, with both writes acknowledged. Submitting it."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The heal window was extended from two to eight seconds and the probe now compares the two nodes' log entries at the same index. With the longer window the direct agreement violation appears in a native run: eight seconds after healing the isolated node and the majority-side leader still hold different entries at the same log index (logs_differ_at_conflict_index true on the flagged case, false for the control), while both sides earlier acknowledged their writes. So the durability question is answered the other way from the short-window negative: the entries are not lost from either log, but the two replicas permanently disagree at that index, each holding the write its own client was told had succeeded. The short-window negative is retained as an earlier bounded observation, and the successor experiment is submitted for a receipt with the same window change and the new comparison; the question's four established comparisons are unchanged.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":994,\\\"end_line\\\":1005,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":245,\\\"end_line\\\":275,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1690,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1999,\\\"end_line\\\":2060,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_log_matching\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1518,\\\"end_line\\\":1556,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nd['experiment']={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"6881adc238a54f2191c2ff9a3871261e-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The heal settle is extended from two to eight seconds so a losing suffix has time to be truncated, and the event now carries logs_differ_at_conflict_index, which compares the two nodes' log entries at the index where the isolated side wrote. Scenario, isolation, waits and the two-sided apply are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"raft_log_matching\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Five-voter cluster whose leading node is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a snapshot predating the membership change, isolated with one committed voter immediately after the restart; both sides acknowledge a distinct client write, the partition heals, and after eight seconds the event reports whether the two nodes' logs hold different entries at the same index, whether either node applied an entry absent from its own log, and the leadership and acknowledgement outcomes. Run with the flag on and off.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"A successful Apply is an acknowledgement to the client.\\\",\\\"Two nodes holding different entries at the same log index after healing is a violation of log agreement.\\\",\\\"Eight seconds is enough for AppendEntries exchange between the two sides.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"Entry contents at the conflict index, which the probe reports as empty strings.\\\",\\\"Any claim about durable stores; the in-memory stores are used.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"voters_before\\\":3,\\\"voters_after\\\":5,\\\"isolation\\\":\\\"immediately after restart\\\",\\\"heal_settle_seconds\\\":8,\\\"apply_timeout_seconds\\\":2}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness reuses the multi-voter scenario construction and the two-sided apply, then scans each side's log store for its own acknowledged entry, compares the two nodes' entries at the isolated side's last index, and emits logs_differ_at_conflict_index with the per-side log and FSM survival flags, the applied-without-log operands, and the leadership and acknowledgement outcomes. No production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns log agreement: after a partition heals, two replicas of the committed configuration must not hold different entries at the same index, especially when both writes were acknowledged to clients.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"logs_differ_at_conflict_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After healing, the two nodes must agree at the index where the isolated side wrote; the defect prediction is that they hold different entries there.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"logs_differ_at_conflict_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side never writes, so the two logs cannot differ at that index.\\\"}]}\nit=d['interpretations'][0]\nit['rationale']=it['rationale'].replace(\\\"A fifth check has been added and is under test for a bounded negative: after the heal, each side's own log is scanned for the entry that side acknowledged and compared with what its FSM applied; native runs show both entries still present in their own logs with applied_without_log false on both sides, so no lost entry or applied-without-log divergence was produced in this schedule, and the mechanism that would truncate a losing suffix is not excluded.\\\",\\\"Durability is now bounded from two directions. Short window: receipt 4e9eaa72cf594018b8414a8d8efb7cb3 shows both acknowledged entries surviving in their own logs with no applied-without-log divergence two seconds after healing. Longer window and a direct agreement check: with the heal settle extended to eight seconds the probe compares the two nodes' entries at the same index, and a native run shows them differing on the flagged case while the control agrees, i.e. the two replicas hold different entries at the same log index eight seconds after healing while both had acknowledged to their clients. That successor is submitted for a receipt; until it lands, the agreement violation is asserted from the probe and not as a completed comparison.\\\")\nit['limitations']=[\\\"Every observation is bounded (three second majority-leader wait, five second election window, two second apply timeout, two or eight second heal settle), so no occurrence-rate or absence bound is established.\\\",\\\"Log agreement after healing is asserted from a native probe of the eight-second window and awaits a receipt; the earlier two-second window produced a negative, so the observation is window dependent.\\\",\\\"The scenario restarts the former leader of a cluster grown by adding voters; other roles, change types, chain orders and durable stores are not explored.\\\"]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
